<refentry xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.2" id="ndm">

	<refmeta>
		<refentrytitle>ndm</refentrytitle>
		<manvolnum>1</manvolnum>
	</refmeta>

	<refnamediv>
		<refname>ndm</refname><refpurpose>the <application>NDManager Plugins</application> are a collection of scripts and tools to process wideband brain signals, video and behavioral events.</refpurpose>
	</refnamediv>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Description</title>
		<para>
			The <application>NDManager Plugins</application> include scripts and tools to help you process data recorded using electrophysiological data acquisition systems: they perform format conversion, resampling and filtering, spike extraction, video tracking, etc.
		</para>
		<para>
			The typical manner to use <application>NDManager Plugins</application> is as follows:
		</para>
		<orderedlist>
			<listitem>
				<para>
					Rename and reorganize your raw data files so that they conform to the naming scheme used by <command>ndm_start</command> (see its manual page for the conventions), and verify that no expected files are missing.
				</para>
			</listitem>
			<listitem>
				<para>
					Create the session parameter file <filename>SESSION.yaml</filename> with <application>NDManager</application>, or copy <filename>templates/template.yaml</filename> from the source tree (templates are YAML), and set the parameters of the steps under <literal>programs:</literal>: numbers of channels, sampling rates, thresholds, etc. The step descriptions <application>NDManager</application> reads are installed in <filename><replaceable>prefix</replaceable>/share/ndmanager/descriptions</filename>. An old XML parameter file can be converted with <command>ndm_xml2yaml</command>.
				</para>
			</listitem>
			<listitem>
				<para>
					Run <command>ndm_start</command>.
				</para>
			</listitem>
		</orderedlist>
		<para>
			This will convert data files, resample, reorder and/or extract brain signals, track LEDs, etc. then concatenate the resulting files before processing spikes (detection, extraction, PCA) and creating LFP files.
		</para>
		<para>
			Please read the manual page for <command>ndm_start</command> for additional information.
		</para>
	</refsect1>

	<refsect1>
		<title>Technical Reference</title>
		<para>
			Briefly, scripts and tools form a kind of pyramid where lower levels (tools) perform simple tasks, while higher levels (scripts) perform progressively more complex and integrated tasks. At the top of the pyramid is <command>ndm_start</command>, which automatically takes care of all processing steps.
		</para>

		<para>
			More precisely:
			<itemizedlist>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Tools perform single, unitary processing steps (conversion, filtering, resampling... see manual page for <command>process</command> for details). Although tools are powerful and flexible, they are command-line programs and are not user-friendly. You should normally not need to run them directly.
					</para>
				</listitem>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						Unitary scripts perform equivalent functions but are easier to use: they read all the necessary parameters from the session parameter file (<filename>SESSION.yaml</filename>), which can be graphically edited using <application>NDManager</application>. They also provide some additional features, such as better feedback (warning and error messages). Similar to tools, you should normally not need to run unitary scripts directly.
					</para>
				</listitem>
				<listitem>
					<para>
						The batch script <command>ndm_start</command> automatically takes care of all the processing steps for a given recording session or collection of sessions.
					</para>
				</listitem>
			</itemizedlist>
		</para>

		<para>
			NOTE: <application>NDManager Plugins</application> assume that the data files are named according to a flexible naming scheme described in the manual page for <command>ndm_start</command>.
		</para>

		<refsect2><title>Batch processing script</title>

			<para>
				This script takes care of all processing steps for a given session or collection of sessions (see the manual page for <command>ndm_start</command> for details).
			</para>

			<variablelist>
				<varlistentry>
					<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_start</command></term>
					<listitem>
						<para>
							perform all processing steps for multiple sets of multiple sessions.
						</para>
					</listitem>
				</varlistentry>
			</variablelist>
		</refsect2>

		<refsect2><title>Unitary processing scripts</title>

			<para>
				Unitary processing scripts take care of a single processing step (conversion, filtering, resampling...) Under normal circumstances, you should not need to use them explicitly: instead, <command>ndm_start</command> will handle all processing steps automatically. However, in special cases where performing a single processing step is required, unitary scripts can be used directly (see their help pages in <application>NDManager</application> for details). The list below names the main ones; <filename>doc/ndmanager-plugins/commands/README.md</filename> in the source tree documents every step.
			</para>

			<variablelist>
				<varlistentry>
					<term>File format conversion</term>
					<listitem>
						<variablelist>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_ncs2dat</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										convert Neuralynx <replaceable>.ncs</replaceable> data files to multiplexed binary (<replaceable>.dat</replaceable>) format.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command>ndm_nev2evt</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										convert Neuralynx <replaceable>.nev</replaceable> files to event format (<replaceable>.evt</replaceable>).
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_nvt2spots</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										convert Neuralynx <replaceable>.nvt</replaceable> tracker files to spots format.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_smi2sts</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										convert Neuralynx <replaceable>.smi</replaceable> video timestamp file to spots timestamps (<replaceable>.sts</replaceable> file).
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_smr2dat</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										convert Spike2 <replaceable>.smr</replaceable> data files to multiplexed binary format.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_smr2evt</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										convert Spike2 <replaceable>.smr</replaceable> data files to event format.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command>ndm_plx2dat</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										convert Plexon <replaceable>.plx</replaceable> / <replaceable>.pl2</replaceable> recordings to multiplexed binary format (plus events).
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command>ndm_aom2dat</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										convert AlphaOmega <replaceable>.mat</replaceable> (HDF5) recordings to multiplexed binary format.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_tsp2sts</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										convert Amplipex <replaceable>.tsp</replaceable> video timestamp file to spots timestamps (<replaceable>.sts</replaceable> file).
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
						</variablelist>
					</listitem>
				</varlistentry>
				<varlistentry>
					<term>Electrophysiological data processing</term>
					<listitem>
						<variablelist>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_resample</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										resample multiplexed binary (<replaceable>.dat</replaceable>) data files.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_mergedat</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										merge simultaneously recorded multiplexed binary (<replaceable>.dat</replaceable>) data files.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_extractchannels</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										extract channels from a multiplexed binary (<replaceable>.dat</replaceable>) data file.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_reorderchannels</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										reorder channels in a multiplexed binary (<replaceable>.dat</replaceable>) data file.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_hipass</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										hi-pass filter a multiplexed binary (<replaceable>.dat</replaceable>) data file (-> <replaceable>.fil</replaceable> file); Butterworth by default, median filter on request.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command>ndm_bandpass</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										band-pass filter instead (median high-pass then FIR low-pass, -> <replaceable>.fil</replaceable>).
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command>ndm_lfp</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										downsample the wideband data to an LFP file.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_setupgroups</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										write the anatomical and spike detection channel groups from the probes listed in the session file.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command>ndm_spikegrouper</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										discover spike detection channel groups from the <replaceable>.fil</replaceable> data.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_detectspikes</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										detect spikes and write the shared timestamps (<replaceable>.res</replaceable>) from a high-pass filtered multiplexed binary (<replaceable>.fil</replaceable>) data file.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_extractspikes</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										extract spike waveforms (<replaceable>.spk</replaceable>) at the timestamps (<replaceable>.res</replaceable>) written by ndm_detectspikes; the extraction engine may differ from the detection engine.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command>ndm_extractspikes_sdiff</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										detect and extract spikes on a spatial derivative (also <command>ndm_extractspikes_stderiv</command>: spatial plus temporal derivative).
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_pca</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										compute principal component analysis (PCA) on spike data for subsequent cluster cutting (-> <replaceable>.fet</replaceable> and <replaceable>.pca</replaceable> files; <command>ndm_pca_stderiv</command> for stderiv spikes).
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command>ndm_klustakwik</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										cluster each spike group with KiloKlustaKwik (-> <replaceable>.clu</replaceable>).
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
						</variablelist>
					</listitem>
				</varlistentry>
				<varlistentry>
					<term>After sorting</term>
					<listitem>
						<variablelist>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_estimatedrift</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										estimate probe drift from curated clusters (-> <replaceable>.drift</replaceable>).
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command>ndm_applydrift</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										apply the drift of one shank to its sibling groups.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_driftcorrect</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										re-featurize spike waveforms to a reference probe position.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_decomposecollisions</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										decompose collisions of two units (-> <replaceable>.col</replaceable>).
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
						</variablelist>
					</listitem>
				</varlistentry>
				<varlistentry>
					<term>Video processing</term>
					<listitem>
						<variablelist>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_extractleds</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										extract LEDs from a video (<replaceable>.mpg</replaceable>, <replaceable>.avi</replaceable>, etc.) or tracker (<replaceable>.nvt</replaceable>) file.
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_transcodevideo</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										transcode a video file (convert to a different codec).
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
						</variablelist>
					</listitem>
				</varlistentry>
				<varlistentry>
					<term>Concatenation</term>
					<listitem>
						<variablelist>
							<varlistentry>
								<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_concatenate</command></term>
								<listitem>
									<para>
										concatenate wideband signals and behavioral events from successive sessions, keeping them synchronized (video frames can later be concatenated and synchronized using the Matlab function <command>spots2pos</command>, which is kept in the source tree but not installed).
									</para>
								</listitem>
							</varlistentry>
						</variablelist>
					</listitem>
				</varlistentry>
			</variablelist>
		</refsect2>

		<refsect2><title>Additional helper scripts</title>

			<para>
				These scripts are not actually part of the <application>NDManager Plugins</application>, but provide useful additional functionality (see their respective manual pages for details).
			</para>

			<variablelist>
				<varlistentry>
					<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_recolorchannels</command></term>
					<listitem>
						<para>
							change channel colors in a XML parameter file.
						</para>
					</listitem>
				</varlistentry>
				<varlistentry>
					<term><command moreinfo="refentry">ndm_xml2yaml</command></term>
					<listitem>
						<para>
							convert an XML parameter file to the YAML session format.
						</para>
					</listitem>
				</varlistentry>
				<varlistentry>
					<term><command moreinfo="refentry">duration</command></term>
					<listitem>
						<para>
							determine the duration and number of samples in one or more data files.
						</para>
					</listitem>
				</varlistentry>
				<varlistentry>
					<term><command moreinfo="refentry">rn</command></term>
					<listitem>
						<para>
							rename a group of files as a numbered file list.
						</para>
					</listitem>
				</varlistentry>
				<varlistentry>
					<term><command moreinfo="refentry">pad</command></term>
					<listitem>
						<para>
							pad numbers in file names with appropriate numbers of '0' to yield a given length
						</para>
					</listitem>
				</varlistentry>
				<varlistentry>
					<term><command moreinfo="refentry">cnt</command></term>
					<listitem>
						<para>
							count unique existing files (or directories) among listed names
						</para>
					</listitem>
				</varlistentry>
			</variablelist>
		</refsect2>
	</refsect1>

